      "codeName": "D18",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "led_r_low"
      ],
      "notes": "RGB LED red channel — GP18, active-low, PWM-dimmable. Confirmed via shop.pimoroni.com/pishop.us Tiny 2350 product page (GP18-GP20 RGB LED, active low) and forums.pimoroni.com RGB LED PWM sample code (TINY2350_LED_R_PIN = 18). Same pin numbering/polarity as the RP2040 sibling variants/rp2040/rp2040/pimoroni_tiny2040/board.json."
    },
    {
      "name": "D19",
      "label": "GPIO19 (Led Green active low)",
      "codeName": "D19",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "led_g_low"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_LED / LED_BUILTIN — RGB LED green channel, GP19, active-low, PWM-dimmable. This board's pins_arduino.h comment states 'Use the Green LED element on pin 19 as LED_BUILTIN' — LED_BUILTIN drives only this one channel of the 3-channel RGB LED, not a standalone single-color LED. Same sources as GPIO18."
    },
