      "capabilities": [
        "digital_input",
        "button"
      ],
      "notes": "BOOTSEL / user button — not declared in this board's pins_arduino.h (no PIN_BUTTON alias), but confirmed via current shop.pimoroni.com/pishop.us Tiny 2350 product pages ('GPIO Pin: GP23', 'Logic: active low', 'use the BOOT button as a user switch') and the recurring 'clever circuitry that lets you use the boot button as a user controllable switch' phrasing already confirmed diode-based on the Tiny 2040 sibling. digital_output/pwm_output deliberately omitted — no vendor source confirms it is electrically safe to drive this BOOT/DFU-select line as an output; matches the conservative precedent set for the Tiny 2040's GPIO23 in variants/rp2040/rp2040/pimoroni_tiny2040/board.json.\nCheck if available on board"
